  nonce: '7638'  # 7638
  message: "Investigated 2026-06-01 for cluster context. Parent set to INV-bazij (P0 pending_validation, stable_id mass collisions). Phase 6 PR3 (ea0154e54f) closed INV-bazij structurally — 60.2% → 0.8% collision rate via name+qualified_name hash inputs at compute_stable_id and py.py::_compute_stable_id. WI-bupim addresses the residual ~0.8% (289 collisions across 95 groups) in two parts: (a) typed-tier make_typed_stable_id callers in 10 mainstream analyzers — mechanical sweep; (b) linker-emitted call_site collisions — needs design call. Sibling of WI-vodin (canonical-id format static check) under the larger INV-tazaj uniqueness META cluster. Doesn't duplicate any preexisting row — it's the residual tail of an in-flight P0."  # 7638
- op: discuss  # 0ad0
  at: '2026-06-02T04:54:12Z'  # 0ad0
  by: agent  # 0ad0
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0ad0
  clock: 4  # 0ad0
  nonce: 0ad0  # 0ad0
  message: "**Pass-24 finding (F24.6) — `export` (50% dup rate) and `call_site` (40% dup rate) kinds have same (path, name, kind) → multiple node IDs.**\n\nFiltering out external_symbol kind (whose `<external>` path makes the triplet degenerate by design), 295/32,615 = 0.904% of nodes share (path, name, kind) with at least one other node. By kind:\n\n| kind | nodes | unique triplets | dup rate |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| export | 20 | 10 | **50.00%** |\n| call_site | 130 | 78 | **40.00%** |\n| function | 7,098 | 7,028 | 0.99% |\n| class | 4,444 | 4,401 | 0.97% |\n| method | 18,290 | 18,264 | 0.14% |\n| variable | 1,609 | 1,608 | 0.06% |\n| file / dependency / interface / project | — | — | 0.00% |\n\n**Most function/class duplicates are legitimate.** Test files frequently redefine local classes per test scenario (`class Args:` defined 8 times in `test_cli_commands.py` for 8 different tests). Route registration patterns also recur (`ws:/ws` function defined at multiple lines in `test_websocket.py`). These ARE real distinct code entities; the IDs include span which differentiates them.\n\n**Export 50% rate is the interesting case.** Bash `export VAR_NAME` declared multiple times in the same script:\n\n```\nscripts/auto-pr declares CI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS at lines 996, 1450, 1472\nscripts/ci-failover declares FORGEJO_TOKEN at lines 158, 204, 214\nscripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh declares CI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS at lines 1354, 1358\n```\n\nEach `export` emits a Symbol node, so 3 declarations of `CI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` → 3 nodes. Re-export of the same variable name is a common bash pattern for subshell-inheritance; graph queries asking \"what does this script export?\" want 1 node per name, not N.\n\n**Call_site 40% rate** has a similar pattern at the call layer (e.g., `DELETE items` call_site at lines 215, 372, 497 in `cache.py` — same SQL string at multiple call sites).\n\n**Cluster context.** Adjacent to WI-bupim's \"~0.8% typed-tier + linker call_site residuals\" but a different surface — bash analyzer + call-site producer treat each occurrence as a distinct Symbol. Either dedup at emit time (1 Symbol per unique name per file, all spans in `meta.declaration_sites`) or schema-declare \"each declaration is a distinct Symbol; consumers must aggregate by name.\"\n\nSame shape as the WI-bupim cluster but at a different layer; documents an additional case in the WI-bupim residual catalog. Pass-24 finding kept here as a residual observation rather than promoted to a new tracker item.\n\n**Lab notebook entry:** `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_06022026_0250_pass24.md`."  # 0ad0
- op: discuss  # 5473
  at: '2026-06-02T05:47:42Z'  # 5473
  by: agent  # 5473
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5473
  clock: 5  # 5473
  nonce: '5473'  # 5473
  message: "Pass-26 stable_id collision direct measurement — INV-bazij is essentially satisfied modulo WI-bupim residual:\n\nPass-26 substrate (/tmp/hg-dogfood-s21/bm.json, post-INV-sugat-closure):\n- 33923 distinct stable_id values across 34117 sha256-form stable_ids\n- 95 stable_ids appear more than once (collide)\n- 289 total nodes share a stable_id with another (collision rate = **0.84%**)\n\nThis is a massive improvement from INV-bazij's original 60.2% collision rate. The recent INV-bazij phase 6 / stable_id_scheme v5 work dropped collision rate by ~71×. The remaining 0.84% matches WI-bupim's \"typed-tier + linker call_site residuals + bash export dup\" scope exactly — pass-24 F24.6 (export 50% dup rate + call_site 40% dup rate at the (path,name,kind) triplet for bash) and pass-21's typed-tier residual are the explainers for the 289 remaining collisions.\n\nTop-10 colliding stable_ids:\n```\n  sha256:fc4f52d59df5d3a5: 13\n  sha256:8edfffc2f65c5215: 12\n  sha256:3cd0dfc7ff321942: 8\n  sha256:c2969cd7f85070ca: 8\n  sha256:28ac219a7c417606: 7\n  sha256:60f4fc62c10e3fb4: 7\n  sha256:72e939f31f34d1cb: 7\n  sha256:84482e30ccf39232: 5\n  sha256:b6775db0478a721b: 5\n  sha256:2b21f4442ba08723: 5\n```\n\nStatus implications:\n- INV-bazij (the parent META \"stable_id mass collisions\") — status `pending_validation` now has concrete substrate-side evidence the issue is essentially fixed (0.84% << 60.2% baseline). Likely candidate for `satisfied` after WI-bupim closes.\n- WI-bupim (the tail covering the ~0.8% residual) — pass-26 confirms 0.84% (consistent with WI-bupim's \"~0.8% typed-tier + linker call_site residuals\" framing). Status quo holds.\n\nNo new tracker action; pass-26 just provides clean quantitative confirmation. This is the \"substrate proves the campaign worked\" narrative point."  # 5473
- op: discuss  # 7869
