  clock: 6  # 7869
  nonce: '7869'  # 7869
  message: "Pass 38 (2026-06-02, dogfooding) — 4 findings batched at WI-bupim cohort decomposition:\n\nF38.B2: Top 5 collision cohorts at --max-files=10 enumerated:\n- SQL parse-artifact: 'SELECT users' 13×, 'SELECT items' 4× — call_site kind, language=None (21+ nodes)\n- kafka-linker placeholder: 'kafka:publish:topic' 8×, 'kafka:publish:user-events' 7×, 'kafka:subscribe:*' 5-7× each (48 nodes)\n- bash export-VAR: FORGEJO_TOKEN 5×, CI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS 4×, usage 4× (26 nodes)\n- HTTP-linker URL-variant: 7 symbols at sha256:28ac219a7c417606 collapsing 'GET /api/users' across 3 URL forms\n- GraphQL placeholder: 'Query.users' 4× (kind=function, language=None)\n\nF38.B3: NEW WI-bupim cohort — GraphQL resolver linker. 4 distinct symbols named 'Query.users' (kind=function) share one stable_id. GraphQL resolver linker emits placeholder symbols without per-resolver disambiguation. Adds graphql-resolver-linker to WI-bupim's known cohort family (previously: typed-tier + linker call_site). The same shape as kafka-linker (which already-existed in WI-bupim scope per pass-36 F36.B4) but for a different placeholder mechanism.\n\nF38.B4: NEW BUG — TypeScript analyzer hash-input-insufficient cross-name collision. 4 distinct stable_ids collapse multiple TS symbols with DIFFERENT names:\n- sha256:f4a7af6e179e8aba: {connect, connectWebSocket, registerServiceWorker, scheduleReconnect} across 2 files\n- sha256:5b1252b57e00fd12: {ItemDetail.render, ItemList.render, TrackerApp.render} across 3 Lit component files\n- sha256:465a58dbfa932b3a: {ItemDetail.onDiscussSubmit, TrackerApp.connectedCallback, ItemDetail.onBack, TrackerApp.onBack}\n- sha256:e067b2ec87edc43c: {ItemDetail.onStatusChange, ItemDetail.onDiscussInput}\n\nThese are NOT name-repetition — distinct symbols with different .name values collide. Hash inputs must be excluding name+path+span+class. Structurally different from bash export-VAR (within-name repetition) or kafka-linker (placeholder template). All 4 TS clusters ALSO collide in ROOT default substrate (per F38.B6), confirming the bug is present at production scale (not a truncation artifact). Adds js_ts.py to WI-bupim's typed-tier callers cohort.\n\nF38.B5: bash has 0 cross-name collisions (negative half of F38.B4). All bash collisions are within-name repetition. Different fix path: bash needs per-statement-line disambiguation; TS needs name/path inclusion in hash inputs. WI-bupim residual cohort warrants multi-mechanism decomposition by linker/analyzer source — bash export-VAR (within-name) + TS qualified_name (cross-name) + kafka placeholder + graphql placeholder + HTTP URL-variant + SQL parse-artifact all sit under WI-bupim with structurally different fix paths."  # 7869
