  new_text: "**Pass-24 finding (F24.6) — call_site 40% dup rate.** (Bash export 50% dup rate migrated to WI-nasil-bovuj per fold-audit Phase 2b.)\n\nFiltering out external_symbol kind (whose `<external>` path makes the triplet degenerate by design), 295/32,615 = 0.904% of nodes share (path, name, kind) with at least one other node. By kind:\n\n| kind | nodes | unique triplets | dup rate |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| export | 20 | 10 | 50.00% (→ WI-nasil) |\n| **call_site** | **130** | **78** | **40.00%** |\n| function | 7,098 | 7,028 | 0.99% |\n| class | 4,444 | 4,401 | 0.97% |\n| method | 18,290 | 18,264 | 0.14% |\n| variable | 1,609 | 1,608 | 0.06% |\n| file / dependency / interface / project | — | — | 0.00% |\n\n**Most function/class duplicates are legitimate.** Test files frequently redefine local classes per test scenario (`class Args:` defined 8 times in `test_cli_commands.py` for 8 different tests). Route registration patterns also recur (`ws:/ws` function defined at multiple lines in `test_websocket.py`). These ARE real distinct code entities; the IDs include span which differentiates them.\n\n**Call_site 40% rate is WI-bupim residual scope** at the call layer (e.g., `DELETE items` call_site at lines 215, 372, 497 in `cache.py` — same SQL string at multiple call sites). Linker-emitted call_site nodes don't carry per-site disambiguation; same shape as the typed-tier residual cohort WI-bupim umbrellas. Either dedup at emit time (1 call_site per unique target per file, all spans aggregated) or schema-declare each call_site as distinct.\n\n**Lab notebook entry:** `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_06022026_0250_pass24.md`."  # 1ea8
  reason: "fold-audit Phase 2b: F24.6 bash export migrated; call_site kept"  # 1ea8
