  new_text: "Pass 38 (2026-06-02, dogfooding) — WI-bupim cohort decomposition findings (F38.B4 TS hash-input bug migrated to WI-zitod-jizal per fold-audit Phase 2b; bash within-name-repetition portion of F38.B5 migrated to WI-nasil-bovuj):\n\nF38.B2: Top 5 collision cohorts at --max-files=10 enumerated:\n- SQL parse-artifact: 'SELECT users' 13×, 'SELECT items' 4× — call_site kind, language=None (21+ nodes)\n- kafka-linker placeholder: 'kafka:publish:topic' 8×, 'kafka:publish:user-events' 7×, 'kafka:subscribe:*' 5-7× each (48 nodes)\n- bash export-VAR: FORGEJO_TOKEN 5×, CI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS 4×, usage 4× (26 nodes — see WI-nasil)\n- HTTP-linker URL-variant: 7 symbols at sha256:28ac219a7c417606 collapsing 'GET /api/users' across 3 URL forms\n- GraphQL placeholder: 'Query.users' 4× (kind=function, language=None)\n\nF38.B3: NEW WI-bupim cohort — GraphQL resolver linker. 4 distinct symbols named 'Query.users' (kind=function) share one stable_id. GraphQL resolver linker emits placeholder symbols without per-resolver disambiguation. Adds graphql-resolver-linker to WI-bupim's known cohort family (previously: typed-tier + linker call_site). The same shape as kafka-linker (which already-existed in WI-bupim scope per pass-36 F36.B4) but for a different placeholder mechanism.\n\nF38.B5 (residual scope): WI-bupim residual cohort warrants multi-mechanism decomposition by linker/analyzer source. Post-Phase 2b decomposition: bash export-VAR within-name (WI-nasil), TS qualified_name cross-name (WI-zitod), kafka placeholder (WI-bupim residual), graphql placeholder (WI-bupim residual via F38.B3), HTTP URL-variant (WI-bupim residual), SQL parse-artifact (WI-bupim residual). Bash and TS broken out as discrete rows; kafka/graphql/HTTP/SQL placeholders remain under WI-bupim umbrella with structurally similar fix-paths (per-emission disambiguation token in hash input)."  # fc40
